# Copy to apps/web/.env for local development.
#
# There is exactly one switch here, and it decides which backend the SPA
# talks to.

# Unset (or anything but "live") in dev → M1's in-memory mock, so the UI is
# clickable with nothing else running. Set to "live" → the real `apps/api`,
# which Vite proxies at /api (see vite.config.ts), so the session cookie is
# first-party exactly as it will be behind Caddy.
#
# Production builds are always live: the mock is behind `import.meta.env.DEV`
# and dynamically imported, so it is not in the production bundle at all.
VITE_API_MODE=live

# Only needed if the API is somewhere other than the Vite proxy's /api —
# which would also mean giving up the same-origin cookie, so prefer the proxy.
# VITE_API_BASE=/api
